<person xml:id="person-heinrich-i"><persName>Heinrich I.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes King/Emperor Heinrich I. (the Fowler), Burggraf Heinrich I. von Plauen (1389-1429), Heinrich I. von Schleiz (1639-1692; 1695-1744), Heinrich I. von Obergreiz (1627-1681; 1693-1714) and a prince born 1803 (printed "I.", transcribed "L." on p. 399).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-ii"><persName>Heinrich II.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Burggraf Heinrich II. von Plauen (1429-1446), Heinrich II. von Gera (1602-1670), Heinrich II. von Burgk (two persons), Heinrich II. von Köstritz (1803-1852), Heinrich II. von Lobenstein (d. 1782) and Heinrich II. von Obergreiz (1696-1722).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-lxii-fuerst-reuss-j-l"><persName>Heinrich LXII. (Fürst Reuß j. L.)</persName><note>Heinrich LXII., Fürst von Reuß-Schleiz und seit 1848 des vereinigten Reuß j. L.; geb. 1785, regierte in Schleiz 1818-1848, im Gesamtland 1848-1854, † 19. Juni 1854 ohne Erben; Bruder und Vorgänger Heinrichs LXVII.</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q73528</idno></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-lxvii-fuerst-reuss-j-l"><persName>Heinrich LXVII. (Fürst Reuß j. L.)</persName><note>Heinrich LXVII., Fürst Reuß j. L.; geb. 20. Okt. 1789, Nachfolger seines Bruders Heinrich LXII. am 19. Juni 1854, † 11. Juli 1867; verheiratet 1820 mit Sophie Adelheid von Reuß-Ebersdorf; Vater Heinrichs XIV.; Umbau des Schlosses Osterstein.</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q215064</idno></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-lxxii-fuerst-reuss-lobenstein-ebersdorf"><persName>Heinrich LXXII. (Fürst Reuß-Lobenstein-Ebersdorf)</persName><note>Heinrich LXXII., Fürst von Lobenstein-Ebersdorf, einziger Sohn Heinrichs LI.; geb. 1797, regierte 1822-1848 (Verzicht am 1. Okt. 1848), † Febr. 1853 in Dresden als letzter männlicher Sproß des Specialhauses Lobenstein; nannte die alte Landesvertretung „verrottet".</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q215069</idno></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-x"><persName>Heinrich X.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Heinrich X. von Lobenstein (1621-1671; see the separate entry "Heinrich X. v. Lobenstein"), Heinrich X. von Ebersdorf (1662-1711) and Prince Heinrich X. (1827-1847, Köstritz).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xi"><persName>Heinrich XI.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Heinrich XI. von Schleiz (1669-1726; see "Heinrich Reuß XI"), Heinrich XI. von Obergreiz/Greiz (1722-1800, first prince of Greiz) and others.</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xii"><persName>Heinrich XII.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Mostly Graf Heinrich XII. von Schleiz (1716-1784; see "Graf Heinrich XII"), but also Prince Heinrich XII. (1829-1866) and short-lived princes in the tables.</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xiv"><persName>Heinrich XIV.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Nine of the eleven mentions denote the reigning prince Heinrich XIV. Reuß j. L. (b. 1832; see the separate entry "Fürst Heinrich XIV"); the others are table cells for Heinrich XIV. of Greiz (1749-1799, p. 401) and a child of Obergreiz (1674-1682, p. 402).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xlii-fuerst-reuss-zu-schleiz"><persName>Heinrich XLII. (Fürst Reuß zu Schleiz)</persName><note>Heinrich XLII., Graf, seit 1806 Fürst Reuß zu Schleiz; geb. 1752 zu Löhma, regierte 1784-1818 (Rheinbund 1807), † 1818; Sohn Heinrichs XII., Vater Heinrichs LXII. und LXVII.</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q16405589</idno></person>
